From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 10:27:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] msm8996-common: LiveDisplay without DisplayModes, as on 22.2

The AIDL sdm LiveDisplay service declares and constructs DisplayModes
unconditionally, and its constructor aborts when the QDCM backend
reports no display modes ("DisplayModes backend not ready, exiting").
This panel has none -- there is no qdcm_calib_data in /vendor/etc, and
the 22.2 manifest declared only IPictureAdjustment.

The abort loop is not cosmetic: IDisplayModes is declared in the VINTF
manifest, so LiveDisplayService's boot-phase handler waits for it
forever ("Waited one second for vendor.lineage.livedisplay.IDisplayModes/
default") inside finishBooting(). sys.boot_completed is set right after
that handler returns, so the UI is up but boot never completes; the first
system_server dies to the Watchdog on the display thread instead.

Opt out of DisplayModes with the soong config the HAL exposes (the same
line device/google/bonito uses), which drops both the constructor and the
VINTF fragment. PictureAdjustment stays.

---
 msm8996.mk | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/msm8996.mk b/msm8996.mk
index 0ab6a5ab..674d8881 100644
--- a/msm8996.mk
+++ b/msm8996.mk
@@ -255,6 +255,11 @@ PRODUCT_PACKAGES += \
     init.recovery.qcom.rc
 
 # LiveDisplay
+# PictureAdjustment only, as on 22.2: this panel has no QDCM display modes (no qdcm_calib_data),
+# and the AIDL sdm service aborts in the DisplayModes constructor instead of skipping it. With
+# IDisplayModes declared but never registered, LiveDisplayService blocks in finishBooting and
+# sys.boot_completed is never set.
+$(call soong_config_set_bool,livedisplay_sdm,enable_dm,false)
 PRODUCT_PACKAGES += \
     vendor.lineage.livedisplay-service.sdm
 
